  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KH-CLA_ Phka Sla Akareach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phka Sla Akareach or The Independent of Phka Sla project aims to encourage and empower women and girls to live on their self-independent concept, combat gender stereotype and social norm that put pressure on single women who want to live independently. It indented to see women and society understand more about women&#x2019;s rights in making decisions and be aware that being single or married is their choice. Change the mindset of the society that judges singleness and the audience would know more about the tipto care about their mental health. They want society to know that judgment or stigma is really effected to other people, especially their mental health. This is to encourage women not to be ashamed that being single. Also, women are aware more of well-being to make their mental health strong so they are strong enough to do decision making. To achieve their main objective, they are using social media content creators, and infographics to raise women&#x2019;s awareness through 10 different content, 3 podcasts episodes will be produced by joining by psychologists, influencers, and other special guests with the purpose to stop bullying old-single ladies, understanding &apos;&apos;Decision making&quot;, and get inspiration, tips, advice on how to taking care of their mental health.2 different physical events are planned to beorganized in Battambang and Phnom Penh which will include a practical mental health workshop, song creation workshop, screening day, and art exhibition.  This 12 months project is targeted to conduct in Battambang province and Phnom Penh city.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodian Living Arts</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 1998, Arn Chorn-Pond began Cambodian Living Arts (CLA) as a simple but powerful project: to find the few remaining master artists who had survived the Khmer Rouge genocide, and support them to start teaching their skills to young people in their communities.

The organization on going objectives to:
- Support the continuity and preservation of Cambodia&apos;s artistic heritage
- Develop the Cambodian arts sector through regional, as well as international exchange and promotion
- Advocate the importantrole of arts and culture

Their strategic goals 2023-2025:
- Enable artists and cultural leaders by providing training, funding, resources and networks
- Create a foundation for civic participation and critical reflection among young people through creativities and expressions
- Increase opportunity for underserved population to participate in and experience with the arts
- Strengthen the ecosystem for the arts by supporting the sustainability of strategic initiatives

CLA&apos;s 6 core values: Caringheart, Open heart, Dedicated heart, Creative heart, Nurturing heart.

Today CLA is one of the leading arts organizations in Cambodia and major key players in the arts eco-system. Their work is based on the belief that the arts are at the heart of a vitalsociety. They envision arts and cultural expression as essential to a thriving future for Cambodia, and their mission is to be a catalyst in a vibrant arts sector, inspiring new generations. Over the last 20 years, they have focused on helping talentedpeople to build and develop careers in the arts, through scholarships, fellowships, and support to troupes and individuals.

Looking forward, they aim to promote creativity and innovation in the arts sector, alongside our new evolving role as a grant-makerto further support the arts ecosystem. They are also working to get more arts and culture education into Cambodian public schools and to increase performance opportunities for Cambodian artists.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
